---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Submit a candidate document" description="Suggest public-interest documents that may be worth archiving on streisandeffect.org.">
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Submission intake</p>
    <h1>Suggest a document for preservation</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Use this page to submit information about documents that may be worth archiving. Do not send files as the first step; send provenance, context, and links so the archive can review whether preservation is appropriate.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section callout warning">
    <h2>No automatic hosting</h2>
    <p>
      A submission is a lead, not approval. The archive should not store or publish every suggested document. Each candidate needs human review for public-interest value, provenance, legal risk, safety, and context.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Where to send a candidate</h2>
    <p>
      Email: <a href="mailto:submissions@streisandeffect.org">submissions@streisandeffect.org</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      This address must be configured before launch. Until then, treat it as the intended public intake location and keep candidate notes locally in the project’s submission-candidate folder.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>What to include</h2>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li>The document title, publisher, and publication date if known.</li>
      <li>The original URL and any Internet Archive or other archived URL.</li>
      <li>Why the document appears to have been removed, hidden, altered, or made difficult to access.</li>
      <li>Why preservation is in the public interest.</li>
      <li>Relevant context, criticism, or rebuttals that should appear near the document.</li>
      <li>Whether you have a copy and how you obtained it.</li>
      <li>Any legal threats, takedown requests, public controversy, or safety concerns connected to it.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>What not to send first</h2>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li>Do not send private personal information.</li>
      <li>Do not send hacked, stolen, or unlawfully obtained material.</li>
      <li>Do not send malware, exploit code, or active tracking files.</li>
      <li>Do not attach large files unless the archive has asked for them.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section metadata-panel">
    <h2>Review checklist</h2>
    <table class="meta-table">
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Public interest</th><td>Does preserving this document help accountability, research, criticism, or historical memory?</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Provenance</th><td>Can the archive identify where the document came from and whether the copy is authentic?</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Context</th><td>Can the archive explain the document without endorsing harmful or contested claims?</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Risk</th><td>Are there legal, privacy, safety, or provider-policy risks that need review before hosting?</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
